---
title: "Advanced Airway and Shock Management"
code: "EMS-181"
category: "emergency-medical-services"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites:
  - "2026/EMS-182"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: Current Virginia EMT and CPR certification as approved by the Virginia Office of EMS."
corequisiteNote: "Co-requisite: EMS 182"
---

Introduces core principles of airway, shock, and resuscitation as outlined by the National Emergency Medical Service Education Standards (NEMSES) within the Advanced EMT curriculum. Provides students with a fundamental knowledge of the Cardiopulmonary system, including its assessment and management of shock. Covers cardiac arrest and post-arrest management. Lecture 1 hour. Total 1 hour per week. Additional course fee applies.
